---
/**
 * The print-only masthead for the one-pager routes.
 *
 * The site header is navigation and is stripped from a printed sheet, which
 * would otherwise leave the flyer with nothing on it identifying who it is
 * from — the one thing a sheet handed to a stranger cannot be missing.
 *
 * It is `display: none` on screen (in `one-pager.css`), which also keeps it out
 * of the accessibility tree, where it would only duplicate the header already
 * above it.
 *
 * NOT the `hidden` attribute, and this is a bug that actually shipped:
 * Tailwind's preflight sets `[hidden] { display: none !important }` inside
 * `@layer base`, and for important declarations the layer cascade runs the
 * other way — a layered `!important` beats an unlayered one. The print rule
 * silently lost to it and the masthead never appeared on the sheet.
 *
 * The logomark is `alt=""` because the wordmark beside it already says
 * "Share Meals"; alt text here would announce the name twice.
 */
---

<div class="print-masthead">
  <img src="/logomark.svg" alt="" width="34" height="34" />
  <span class="print-wordmark">Share Meals</span>
  <span class="print-url">sharemeals.org</span>
</div>
